MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Capacitors and larger breadboards feel like useful next purchases because they support the circuit experiments reflected in my mini breadboards, PCB supplies, and relay module.",
    "The connector kit fits my need to make removable wiring connections for PCB and power projects, provided its connectors match my parts."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The three filament recommendations assume I need 3D printing supplies, but my purchases do not establish that I own or use a printer.",
    "The stepper motor requires a motion project I do not currently have. Infrared parts, a thermostat, and a large transistor assortment interest me, but interest alone does not give me a reason to buy them now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in hands-on electronics seems to have been stretched into an interest in 3D printing and CNC projects.",
    "The recommendations seem to assume that any electronic component assortment would be useful to me, even when I have no particular circuit requiring it."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am more likely to choose supplies that extend my existing breadboard, PCB, and wiring work than parts that require starting a different kind of project.",
    "Compatibility and a concrete use matter to me: a connector must fit my parts, and a specialized sensor or controller needs an actual application before I would buy it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my circuit-building interests but extended them too broadly into printing supplies and specialized parts without an established need."
}
